Source: otek-perfex-linux-tracker
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ömer Teknoloji <support@otek.today>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.0

Package: otek-perfex-linux-tracker
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-glib-2.0, gir1.2-adw-1, libglib2.0-bin
Recommends: gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1
Description: Passive focus-based time tracker for Perfex CRM
 Tracks which window/browser tab has focus for the duration of a work
 session against one Perfex CRM task, then submits the reconciled result
 as a batch of timesheet entries when the session is stopped - instead of
 requiring a manual stop/start on every context switch.
 .
 Requires the "window-calls-extended" GNOME Shell extension to read the
 focused window on Wayland. That extension is not packaged in apt and is
 NOT a dependency of this package (GNOME Shell extensions aren't
 apt-installable) - install it separately from extensions.gnome.org or
 https://github.com/hseliger/window-calls-extended. This app detects its
 absence at startup and shows an actionable message rather than failing
 silently.
 .
 The optional top-bar tray icon (Start/Stop/Show/Quit) runs in a small
 separate GTK3 helper subprocess (perfex_tracker/tray_helper.py) using
 AyatanaAppIndicator3 with a real Gtk.Menu - the same library combination
 (confirmed by inspecting real working installations, not guessed) used
 by the Upwork desktop app, VS Code, Zoom, and OnlyOffice/Jitsi on Linux.
 It needs the gir1.2-gtk-3.0 and gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1 packages
 above AND GNOME Shell's own "AppIndicator and KStatusNotifierItem
 Support" extension (also not apt-installable, install from
 extensions.gnome.org) to actually render in the top bar. Neither
 dependency is required for the app to run - without them it simply runs
 window-only, no tray icon.
 .
 X11 is not supported - this app is Wayland-only by design.
